sor-product","def-sheaf-hom","def-pullback-module-ringed-spaces","thm-pullback-pushforward-module-adjunction","lem-pullback-modules-right-exact","def-gluing-datum-sheaves","thm-gluing-sheaves","thm-gluing-ringed-and-locally-ringed-spaces","rem-inverse-image-versus-pullback","ex-direct-image-open-immersion","cex-extension-by-zero-differs-direct-image","ex-skyscraper-sheaf-exact-sequence","cex-global-sections-not-right-exact","ex-ringed-space-continuous-functions","cex-ringed-space-map-not-locally-ringed","ex-pullback-free-module","ex-glue-line-bundle-transition-functions","cex-presheaf-cokernel-needs-sheafification"],"conventions":[{"convention":"An irreducible space is nonempty; an irreducible subset is irreducible in its subspace topology.","fixed_by":"def-irreducible-topological-space-and-subset","matters_for":["thm-irreducible-closed-subsets-and-prime-ideals","thm-irreducible-components-and-minimal-primes"]},{"convention":"Noetherian means ACC on opens, equivalently DCC on closed sets, with the displayed chains indexed from 0.","fixed_by":"def-noetherian-topological-space","matters_for":["thm-noetherian-ring-has-noetherian-spectrum","cor-noetherian-spectrum-has-finitely-many-irreducible-components"]},{"convention":"A specialisation of x is a point y in the closure of {x}; x is then a generalisation of y.","fixed_by":"def-specialisation-and-generic-point","matters_for":["cor-specialisation-order-is-prime-inclusion","cor-spectrum-is-t-zero","lem-support-is-specialisation-closed","ex-zariski-spectrum-not-hausdorff"]},{"convention":"On this page, an affine open in a classical affine variety means a principal open D_X(f).","fixed_by":"def-affine-open-subset-classical-variety","matters_for":["thm-function-field-independent-affine-open","def-rational-map-varieties","lem-rational-map-equivalence-transitive","thm-rational-maps-to-affine-variety-function-field"]},{"convention":"A rational map is an equivalence class of morphisms on nonempty affine opens, with equality witnessed on a nonempty affine open of the overlap.","fixed_by":"def-rational-map-varieties","matters_for":["lem-rational-map-equivalence-transitive","def-domain-of-definition-rational-map","lem-dominant-map-pullback-function-fields","thm-rational-maps-to-affine-variety-function-field","def-birational-equivalence-varieties"]},{"convention":"For an open inclusion, extension by zero consists of sections whose support is closed in the ambient test open; it is not generally the direct image.","fixed_by":"def-extension-by-zero-abelian-sheaf","matters_for":["thm-extension-by-zero-adjunction-exactness","cex-extension-by-zero-differs-direct-image"]},{"convention":"A morphism of locally ringed spaces has stalk maps sending the source maximal ideal into the target maximal ideal.","fixed_by":"def-morphism-locally-ringed-spaces","matters_for":["lem-local-homomorphism-residue-field-map","cex-ringed-space-map-not-locally-ringed"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"lem-zariski-closed-set-axioms","statement":"The subsets V(I) of Spec(R), as I ranges over the ideals of R, define a topology on Spec(R).","used_by":["lem-distinguished-opens-cover-every-open","cor-spectrum-is-a-contravariant-topological-functor","lem-quotient-spectrum-map-is-closed","lem-localisation-spectrum-map-homeomorphism-onto-image"]},{"id":"thm-prime-spectrum-is-compact","statement":"Assume the Axiom of Choice. For every commutative ring R, Spec(R) is compact.","used_by":["cor-every-distinguished-open-is-compact"]},{"id":"thm-irreducible-closed-subsets-and-prime-ideals","statement":"For nonempty closed Z in Spec(R), Z is irreducible iff its radical defining ideal is prime; then it has that ideal as its unique generic point.","used_by":["thm-irreducible-components-and-minimal-primes"]},{"id":"lem-clopen-subset-gives-idempotent-decomposition","statement":"For clopen C in Spec(R), there is an idempotent e with C=V(e)=D(1-e) and complementary part V(1-e)=D(e).","used_by":["cor-spectrum-connected-iff-no-nontrivial-idempotents"]},{"id":"thm-global-regular-functions-affine-variety-coordinate-ring","statement":"For a classical affine variety X, evaluation induces k[X] ≅ O_X(X).","used_by":["def-morphism-classical-varieties","thm-affine-morphisms-coordinate-ring-anti-equivalence","lem-morphism-equality-on-dense-open"]},{"id":"thm-affine-morphisms-coordinate-ring-anti-equivalence","statement":"For classical affine varieties X,Y, Mor(X,Y) is canonically Hom_{k-alg}(k[Y],k[X]), contravariantly with respect to composition.","used_by":["cor-affine-algebraic-set-coordinate-duality-complete","lem-dominant-map-pullback-function-fields","thm-rational-maps-to-affine-variety-function-field","cex-birational-does-not-imply-isomorphic","cex-regular-bijection-not-isomorphism-cusp"]},{"id":"thm-local-ring-affine-variety-localization","statement":"For x in a classical affine variety X, O_{X,x} is canonically isomorphic to k[X]_{m_x}.","used_by":["def-residue-field-classical-point","def-rational-function-regular-at-point","ex-local-ring-affine-line-at-origin"]},{"id":"lem-dominant-map-pullback-function-fields","statement":"A dominant rational map η:X dashedrightarrow Y induces an injective k-algebra homomorphism η*:k(Y)→k(X), independent of representative and functorial.","used_by":["thm-rational-maps-to-affine-variety-function-field"]},{"id":"thm-rational-maps-to-affine-variety-function-field","statement":"Dominant rational maps X dashedrightarrow Y correspond canonically to injective k-field homomorphisms k(Y)→k(X).","used_by":["thm-birational-equivalence-function-fields"]},{"id":"def-inverse-image-presheaf-and-sheaf","statement":"The inverse image sheaf f^{-1}G is the sheafification of the neighbourhood-colimit inverse-image presheaf.","used_by":["thm-inverse-direct-image-adjunction","lem-stalk-inverse-image-sheaf","def-restriction-sheaf-open-subspace","def-pullback-module-ringed-spaces"]},{"id":"thm-exactness-of-sheaves-stalkwise","statement":"A sequence of sheaves of abelian groups is exact iff its sequence at every stalk is exact.","used_by":["thm-extension-by-zero-adjunction-exactness","lem-pullback-modules-right-exact","ex-skyscraper-sheaf-exact-sequence"]},{"id":"def-pullback-module-ringed-spaces","statement":"For a morphism of ringed spaces, f*G=O_X tensor_{f^{-1}O_Y} f^{-1}G.","used_by":["thm-pullback-pushforward-module-adjunction","lem-pullback-modules-right-exact","ex-pullback-free-module","rem-inverse-image-versus-pullback"]},{"id":"thm-gluing-sheaves","statement":"Compatible local sheaves on an open cover glue uniquely up to unique isomorphism.","used_by":["thm-gluing-ringed-and-locally-ringed-spaces","ex-glue-line-bundle-transition-functions"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"cor-affine-closed-points-detect-radicals","used_for":"Maximal ideals detect radical ideals in the closed-point-density corollary.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-nilradical-as-intersection-of-primes","used_for":"Idempotent and connectedness arguments.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-residue-field-of-a-localisation-at-a-prime","used_for":"Residue-field identification at a classical point.","opened":true},{"id":"def-abelian-category","used_for":"Abelian-category structure of sheaf categories.","opened":true},{"id":"def-affine-variety-classical","used_for":"Classical affine variety convention for regular functions.","opened":true},{"id":"def-compact-space","used_for":"Open-cover compactness of spectra and distinguished opens.","opened":true},{"id":"def-connected-space","used_for":"Connected-spectrum criterion.","opened":true},{"id":"def-coordinate-ring-affine-algebraic-set","used_for":"Coordinate-ring, morphism, and rational-map constructions.","opened":true},{"id":"def-exact-sequence-and-short-exact-sequence-in-an-abelian-category","used_for":"Definition of exact sheaf sequences.","opened":true},{"id":"def-field-of-fractions","used_for":"Function-field definition.","opened":true},{"id":"def-flat-and-faithfully-flat-modules-and-ring-maps","used_for":"Flat-stalk exactness criterion for pullback.","o